    {
      "url": "https://github.com/CraigHutchinson/BikeLab/issues/52#issuecomment-6594285597",
      "body": "Correction to this issue's wording from paired measurement: at the level-edge tie the native split is about **0.82 / 0.18** (mean deep-node weight 0.8167 over a resting run; `CONTACT_GAP` gives 0.837), not the whole force on the deeper node. Read it as \"a discontinuous split that doesn't match the gap gradient\". The suggested remedy, a tread law continuous along the edge, stands: see #73, where a soft minimum of the two node gaps settles and converges at first order."
    }
